<!----><!---->                  

    <div class="article-main__content" data-test-id="publishing-text-block">
        <p>
          <span class>Another typical thing (something that happened today, so it's pretty fresh): I asked it to fix a table where one of the attributes was not filled for an element. I asked, "Please add this to this other element." What I meant was, "Go to the backend, find this kind of item, and put the correct data." What the LLM did was it just changed the UI and put some JavaScript stuff that was kind of guessing what the content would have been. It was missing the kind of content. I had to say, "No, not here; in the backend," and then it was able to do that by </span><span class="font-[700]">guiding</span><span class> it.</span><!---->
        </p>
